1
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:12,240
We go to work. We pay bills. We scroll. We compete.

2
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:20,093
We call exhaustion adulthood, anxiety responsibility,

3
00:00:21,093 --> 00:00:28,373
isolation independence, and endless accumulation success.

4
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:35,807
We pretend the picture is coherent.

5
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:42,507
Let us be honest about why.

6
00:00:43,507 --> 00:00:48,867
Marketing fills every space we look at.

7
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:56,400
Screens compete for every minute of our attention.

8
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:02,547
Our attention has become the product.

9
00:01:03,547 --> 00:01:08,587
Money speaks, and most of us listen.

10
00:01:09,587 --> 00:01:16,767
And slowly, we stop caring for each other.

11
00:01:18,967 --> 00:01:24,540
An unresolved thought could change sleep,

12
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:32,180
muscle tension, digestion, attention, and behavior.

13
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:40,807
Worth becomes achievement. Rest becomes laziness.

14
00:01:41,807 --> 00:01:47,593
Success may bring relief, but only briefly.

15
00:01:48,593 --> 00:01:53,740
Like filling a cup with a hole in it.

16
00:01:54,740 --> 00:02:03,307
A persistent sense that something essential is missing.

17
00:02:05,507 --> 00:02:12,360
Culture arrives through language, permitted emotions,

18
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:19,680
authority, admired people, and expected futures.

19
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:27,960
Schools, religions, entertainment, work, law, and markets

20
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:33,127
carry it into daily life.

21
00:02:34,127 --> 00:02:40,233
Much of it is absorbed before it can be named.

22
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:46,593
You inherited a painting already begun.

23
00:02:47,593 --> 00:02:54,447
We are not immune to our culture or our surroundings.

24
00:02:55,447 --> 00:03:02,447
[DOT proposes] This culture works against human development.

25
00:03:03,447 --> 00:03:08,747
None of that is your fault.

26
00:03:09,747 --> 00:03:17,000
But undoing it is your responsibility.

27
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,467
So where do you begin?

28
00:03:26,467 --> 00:03:32,040
The most immediate fact of your existence

29
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:36,940
is not a measurement.

30
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:45,120
It is that you are here to experience one.

31
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:51,153
My name is Henok.

32
00:03:52,153 --> 00:03:56,873
I don’t claim to know everything.

33
00:03:57,873 --> 00:04:05,053
But I feel the erosion. I see the despair.

34
00:04:06,053 --> 00:04:12,480
I pursued these questions while raising a family,

35
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:19,413
carrying debt, and making mistakes.

36
00:04:20,413 --> 00:04:26,093
I have spent my career in software and AI.

37
00:04:27,093 --> 00:04:33,627
Now I am stepping away from it to share this work.

38
00:04:34,627 --> 00:04:39,453
I call it Digital Organism Theory.

39
00:04:40,453 --> 00:04:45,920
I believe we need a cultural revolution,

40
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:53,247
and DOT aims to be its foundation.

41
00:04:55,847 --> 00:04:59,480
[DOT proposes] You are Little c.

42
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:07,440
[DOT proposes] Your living body is your interface to a Reality Frame.

43
00:05:08,440 --> 00:05:15,613
[DOT proposes] Like a musician and an instrument: joined, not the same.

44
00:05:21,413 --> 00:05:27,413
[DOT proposes] This world, RF₀, is an experience laboratory.

45
00:05:28,413 --> 00:05:33,773
[DOT proposes] Its rules turn experience into lessons.

46
00:05:35,973 --> 00:05:42,507
Conditioning is real. Conditioning is not essence.

47
00:05:43,507 --> 00:05:50,253
A river is shaped by its banks. It is not the banks.

48
00:05:51,253 --> 00:05:58,000
What matters is what Little c does with the opening.

49
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:07,173
Freedom is participation in the creation of possibility.

50
00:06:10,373 --> 00:06:22,000
Digital Organism Theory

51
00:06:12,907 --> 00:06:22,000
A school of thought for examining experience.
